WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.190
How cleaning products work, and a production room that keeps you safe.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.280
This is the video for module 1: Cleaning Science and a Safe Production Room.

3
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:15.940
Every product in this course does one of three jobs. It lifts dirt, like grease and food.

4
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:21.850
It dissolves deposits, like limescale, rust stains and urine scale.

5
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.040
Or it kills germs on a surface.

6
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:34.560
When you understand these jobs, you make fewer mistakes, sell the right product to each customer, and write honest directions on the label.

7
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:47.550
Oil and water do not mix. A surfactant is a molecule with two ends. One end pushes into the grease, the other stays in the water, and with rubbing the grease floats away in the rinse.

8
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:59.380
The pH scale runs from 0 to 14, and 7 is neutral. Grease on clothes and floors needs an alkaline cleaner, about pH 9 to 11.

9
00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:04.280
Mineral scale in toilets needs acid, about pH 2.

10
00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:08.830
And germs need a disinfectant, used after cleaning.

11
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:21.900
One warning. BKC, a disinfectant, has a positive charge. LAS and SLES have a negative charge. Mixed together they cancel each other and form a cloudy, useless mess.

12
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:26.590
For example, Ngozi runs a small guest house in Owerri.

13
00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.710
Her kitchen floors are greasy.

14
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:34.950
Grease needs an alkaline cleaner, so you recommend the floor cleaner in warm water with a scrubbing brush.

15
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.430
That uses chemistry, action and temperature together.

16
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:51.140
Her toilets have yellow-brown rings. That is mineral scale, which needs acid. Leave the toilet cleaner for 10 minutes before brushing. Time does the work chemistry alone cannot.

17
00:01:52.390 --> 00:02:04.480
Her towels look grey. Borehole water is often hard, and the minerals waste the surfactant. So you recommend the laundry detergent with soda ash, which softens the water, plus a soak.

18
00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:14.930
Ask every supplier for the safety data sheet and the certificate of analysis, which states the strength. Weigh each delivery and record the lot number.

19
00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:25.860
Then store in four zones with a gap between them: acids, alkalis, bleach on its own, and flammables like isopropyl alcohol away from heat and flame.

20
00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:39.700
Never build a formula on a material of unknown strength. Never put chemicals in a water or soft-drink bottle, because people have drunk them by mistake. And keep powders sealed and off the floor.

21
00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:54.360
Most injuries happen while weighing concentrates, dissolving caustic soda, or pouring one liquid into another. So splash goggles and gloves go on first. Ordinary glasses do not protect from the side.

22
00:02:55.610 --> 00:03:03.890
Caustic soda goes into cold water slowly, never water onto caustic soda. It heats strongly. Never use aluminium.

23
00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:07.830
LABSA also goes into water, while you stir.

24
00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:15.540
Add the caustic solution to the diluted acid slowly, in portions, because neutralising makes heat.

25
00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:20.160
And label every bucket, even if it is only for an hour.

26
00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:33.720
The rule in every module: bleach with acid releases chlorine gas, and bleach with ammonia releases toxic chloramine gases. Never let them share a container, drain or toilet.

27
00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:46.750
For eyes or skin, rinse with running water for at least 15 minutes. Hold the eyelids open, then go to a clinic with the product label. Do not use vinegar to neutralise a splash.

28
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:53.440
If swallowed, do not make the person vomit. Rinse the mouth and get medical help at once.

29
00:03:54.690 --> 00:04:01.600
If products have mixed and made gas, leave the room for fresh air at once, and get help for any coughing or burning.

30
00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:03.850
To remember.

31
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.890
Match the product to the dirt.

32
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.290
Use time, action and temperature in your directions.

33
00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.600
Know the strength of every material.

34
00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:15.000
Add caustic soda and LABSA to water, slowly.

35
00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.980
And bleach never meets acids or ammonia.

36
00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:30.450
Now map the dirt in one building you know, build your raw-material register, and set up your safety station with the first-aid steps on the wall. Continue with the lessons below.
